<div id="2026-11-13-ency-hermes-failover" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-13 — Encyclopedia agent uses the Hermes model order</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The encyclopedia agent no longer stops on SuperGrok <code>grok-4.6</code>. A non-code SuperGrok hop is <code>grok-4.7</code>. When that allowance is gone, the ency purpose walks <code>hermes_fallback_chain</code> (particle-1, then luna inside the OpenRouter caps, then free). particle-1 stays usable when the shared day cap is full, same as Hermes. The classifier no longer treats $1.65 as the OpenRouter day cap; it uses the shared cap file.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The last Health Kitchen call pinned <code>grok-4.6</code> and never tried the models that still have budget. There is no reason to prefer 4.6 over 4.7. x.ai cash (API key) stays off until a daily cap is set.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Model/AI2/Router.pm</code>, <code>Model/AI2/Chat.pm</code>, <code>Util/AI/ModelChains.pm</code>, <code>Model/AI2/Provider/Grok.pm</code></p>
</div>
